{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["לא ימיש — the Holy One, blessed be He: it is in the causative pattern, 'he caused others to move' (ממיש), but לא ימוש ספר התורה is active voice."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "Rashbam contrasts the hif'il (causative) form here — implying 'he did not cause [the pillars] to depart' — with the simple active (pa'al) form used in Joshua 1:8. His glosses are highly compressed; the sense is that לא ימיש is causative ('he did not cause to move away'), unlike the pa'al לא ימוש."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:24.145285695Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}